# Author file signature (HTML / CSS)

When **creating** a new `.html` or `.css` file **anywhere in this repository**, add the studio author signature as a **top-of-file comment**.

## Exact signatures

### CSS (line 1)

```css
/*'bosquestudio','Mariano Montini / Rocio Mio'*/
```

### HTML (immediately after `<!doctype html>`)

```html
<!doctype html>
<!--'bosquestudio','Mariano Montini / Rocio Mio'-->
```

Keep `<!doctype html>` as the first line for compatibility; the signature comment is the next line.

## Rules

- Match the signature **exactly** (spacing and quotes as shown).
- Place it at the top before other file comments, imports/`<link>` notes, or section blocks.
- After the signature, keep visually separated sections with abbreviated comments (`/* What - does */` in CSS; `<!-- What - does -->` in HTML when non-trivial).
- Do **not** add this signature when only editing an existing file that already has content (unless the file is brand-new / empty in the same change).
- If a brand-new HTML/CSS file is created without the signature, add it before finishing the change.
- **Skip** generated or tool-owned outputs (`dist/`, `build/`, `.next/`, `coverage/`, `node_modules/`, and scaffolds that overwrite owned files).
- This signature is for **HTML and CSS only**. For TS/JS/JSX/TSX use `author-js-ts-file-signature.mdc` (different string).
